1005c1005
<     "text": "Plug in (up) or cut (down) the switch cables of machines or of single NICs. Returns the port and link state per NIC, with the port's switch when the lab has several. A cable already as asked is left alone. A NIC that is unplugged goes into the lowest free port of switch0, and plug puts it in any. The cables of a machine that is off can be cut or plugged in; their links come up when it boots. A port names the cable in it (lan:3), also one between switches."
---
>     "text": "Plug in (up) or cut (down) the cables of machines or of single NICs. A port names the cable in it (lan:3), also one between switches. One already as asked is left alone. An unplugged NIC goes into the lowest free port of switch0. A machine that is off takes it too: its links come up when it boots. The options set the cables' conditions, alike in both directions: one left out stays, and a cut, a move or a reboot keeps them. Returns each cable's port and link, and with an option its conditions."
